			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T22:09:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodules — bridged editor state, diagnostics, theme, and breakpoint event pipeline\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky submodules to complete the Mountain-to-Cocoon notification relay for six extension API surfaces that were previously renderer-only.\n\nCocoon adds Notification/Handler.ts cases for `$acceptDiagnosticsChanged`, `$acceptVisibleEditorsChanged`, `$acceptTabsChanged`, `$acceptVisibleRangesChanged`, `$acceptTextEditorOptionsChanged`, and `$acceptActiveColorTheme` — each pumping the Mountain notification through the matching Emitter channel consumed by extension subscribers. The `$acceptTabsChanged` handler caches tab-group snapshots on `__tabGroups` so synchronous `window.tabGroups.all` getters reflect current state.\n\nMountain fans five notification types back to Cocoon: `$acceptActiveColorTheme` in ThemesSet.rs on theme switch, `$acceptVisibleEditorsChanged`/`$acceptTabsChanged`/`$acceptVisibleRangesChanged`/`$acceptTextEditorOptionsChanged` in WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs forwarding Sky payloads, `$acceptDiagnosticsChanged` in Diagnostics.rs after Set/Clear calls, and `$onDidChangeBreakpoints` in DebugLifecycle.rs for breakpoint mutations.\n\nSky bridges four Monaco/workbench event streams through the IPC layer: `onDidScrollChange` (debounced to ~16 fps) emits visible ranges, `onDidChangeConfiguration` emits options changes, `onDidVisibleEditorsChange` emits the URI list of visible editors, and `onDidChangeActiveGroup`/`onDidAddGroup`/`onDidRemoveGroup` emit tab-group snapshots. All IPC calls are wrapped in try/catch so render failures never interrupt the UI pipeline.\n\nVS Code API subscribers inside Cocoon — `languages.onDidChangeDiagnostics`, `window.onDidChangeVisibleTextEditors`, `window.tabGroups.onDidChangeTabs`, `window.onDidChangeTextEditorVisibleRanges`, `window.onDidChangeTextEditorOptions`, `window.onDidChangeActiveColorTheme`, and `debug.onDidChangeBreakpoints` — now fire correctly for all extensions.",
			"SHA": "c378308300e06748e4f3c0b7662a01626242c877"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T21:54:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodules — command execution notification relay\n\nRelay executed command notifications from Mountain to Cocoon so that `vscode.commands.onDidExecuteCommand` callbacks fire inside Node.js extensions.\n\nCocoon replaces the dead `@tauri-apps/api/event`.listen call (which never fires without `window.__TAURI__`) with a subscription to the `commands.executed` Emitter channel, fed by two sources: the `$acceptCommandExecuted` Vine notification from Mountain and local command routes in Commands/Namespace.ts for extension-to-extension `executeCommand` calls. Also extends the `viewId` dual-key resolution strategy (established for `setHtml`/`postMessage`) to five more webview mutators — `dispose`, `setTitle`, `setIconPath`, `setOptions`, `reveal` — so panel mutations arriving before the workbench mounts the IOverlayWebview still reach their target.\n\nMountain dual-emits `$acceptCommandExecuted` over Vine when a command is invoked via `sky://command/execute`, alongside the existing Tauri event that reaches the renderer. The Vine notification is fire-and-forget — failure is non-fatal since renderer-side observers are already notified. Adds the `tauri::Emitter` trait import in CreateEffectForRequest/Commands.rs to satisfy the compiler.\n\nExtension `onDidExecuteCommand` hooks now fire correctly, webview panel mutations during mount race conditions resolve via the viewId fallback, and Cocoon's Terminal/Service.ts is marked deprecated pending vertical-split cleanup.",
			"SHA": "69826df910f62df0c9a34707500640a4dfddc7fc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T21:39:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance Element submodules — webview first-paint race, unhandled IPC notifications\n\nAdvance Cocoon and Mountain submodules to fix a webview panel first-paint race condition and add four IPC notification handlers that were missing from the Mountain dispatch table.\n\nCocoon sends `viewId: ViewType` alongside `handle` in the `webview.setHtml` and `webview.postMessage` request payloads. During first-paint, the `webview.create` acknowledgement can arrive before the workbench's `IOverlayWebview` instantiation has bound the handle to a WebviewInput, causing the initial `setHtml` to land in `ParkedHtml` and `postMessage` to miss its target. Sending both identifiers provides a fallback viewType-keyed lookup in Sky's `InstallWebview.ts` resolution. Also deprecates the `MountainGRPCClientLayer` Effect-TS service tag with documentation pointing consumers to canonical wire-method names.\n\nMountain forwards four previously unhandled IPC notification types: `ScanPathConfigure` to scan `~/.land/extensions` alongside the FIDDEE user directory for pre-migration extension discovery; `debug.dap-response` from Cocoon inline-implementation adapters to the workbench via `sky://debug/dap-message`, enabling the RawDebugSession sequencer to correlate DAP responses by `request_seq`; `setStatusBarText` mutations from extension StatusBarItem `text()` setters, which previously froze status bar text after initial create; and `terminate_task`/`Task.Terminate` to the extension host task service, allowing `vscode.tasks.executeTask().terminate()` to stop running tasks with a graceful fallback.\n\nWebview panels now render correctly on first paint, status bar text updates dynamically, DAP debug sessions receive response correlation, extension task cancellation works end to end, and pre-migration extension directories are discovered on clean installs.",
			"SHA": "285ddc3a49aaf06e7d41b02eba8b9cab74c580eb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T21:29:20Z",
